    <!-- Reading and Notes. Same 24 × 24 box and stroke-only construction as the
         rest of the rail, so the two new sections sit in the family rather than
         announcing themselves as additions. Reading is the dictionary's open book
         with a ribbon rather than a second spine, which is what tells the two rail
         items apart at 18 px; a note is a sheet with a folded corner and two rules. -->
    <Geometry x:Key="WlIconReading">M12,7 C10.5,5.5 8.4,4.8 4.6,4.8 V17.4 C8.4,17.4 10.5,18.1 12,19.6 C13.5,18.1 15.6,17.4 19.4,17.4 V4.8 C15.6,4.8 13.5,5.5 12,7 Z M12,7 V19.6 M15.6,4.9 V11.2 L17.5,9.8 L19.4,11.2 V4.9</Geometry>
